<title>ITALY: Italy to offer tax breaks to firms that reinvest.</title>
<headline>Italy to offer tax breaks to firms that reinvest.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's industry minister Luigi Bersani on Tuesday said that there would be tax breaks from 1998 to Italian companies that reinvest profits back into their own businesses.</p>
<p>&quot;In 1998, I hope to start to lighten the tax burden for those (companies) that reinvest in their businesses,&quot; Bersani said while attending a conference.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
